      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T11:40:42Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, verified StoneVault source, creation transaction, runtime, and commit-pinned reproduction. rollToNextRound is externally callable without an authorization modifier, and the attacker invokes it between an 8,600 ETH deposit and withdrawal. The vault returns 8,617.073005336909691789 ETH, an exact 17.073005336909691789 ETH net loss. StoneVault is a direct deployment whose runtime hash is 0xe001dc7517aedabacb179b8de2cb2c7aece40d83078ff51843b4344b79d73e51 at deployment block 18203833 and immediately before exploit block 18523441. Executable code terminates at byte 0x2902; apparent DELEGATECALL and CREATE2 bytes after that boundary are unreachable appended compiler data. The exploit trace contains no DELEGATECALL from StoneVault."
